Since site v2.21.0 the app's pictures have a gap at the top and the bottom in the screen's
own colour: the gallery draws no status bar, so the page's title sat on the frame's top
edge and was clipped by its rounded corners, and the last row ran into the bottom. The
render is scaled to fit the height between, centred, with the sides in the same colour.
The gaps were 56px at the top and 32px at the bottom, which left the render 741 wide and
20px empty at each side; site v2.25.2 took them to 12px each, and since v2.25.5 the top is
24px and the bottom 12px (1700 between, 764 wide, 8px at each side), both at the owner's
asking. Home's top-left avatar stays inside the roundest corner the site draws (the features
gallery's small frames): look at those frames before taking the top any lower.

No WebP encoder is installed on this machine; the PNGs were scaled and encoded by headless
Chrome's canvas (toDataURL('image/webp', 0.9)), one page per picture.

step1-3 are the phone's own install dialogs, photographed on LB_Clean; they are the same
pictures as before, only re-encoded from PNG to WebP.
